1311
01:06:52,854 --> 01:06:53,954
いつまでやる？
How long does this go on?

1312
01:06:54,454 --> 01:06:55,954
にょっき！
Pop!

1313
01:06:57,304 --> 01:06:58,304
いつまでやる？
How long does this go on?

1314
01:06:57,404 --> 01:07:00,604
[Title: 第97問]
[Title: Question 97]

1315
01:06:58,354 --> 01:06:59,804
でも上手かも。
I'm pretty good though.

1316
01:07:00,904 --> 01:07:02,554
正解は何なのじゃ？
What's the right answer here?

1317
01:07:02,954 --> 01:07:04,354
すや、すや、すや。
Snooze, snooze, snooze.

1318
01:07:04,804 --> 01:07:06,254
え、寝てるよ子供。
Hey, the baby is sleeping.

1319
01:07:07,004 --> 01:07:08,454
出ない方がいいんじゃない？
Shouldn't I stay inside?

1320
01:07:12,054 --> 01:07:13,104
あ、あ、あ！
Ah, ah, ah!

1321
01:07:13,404 --> 01:07:14,804
あ、でも出てる。
Oh, I'm coming out anyway.

1322
01:07:16,204 --> 01:07:19,154
出ない方がいいんじゃない？子供寝てるなら、出ない方がいいんじゃない？
Shouldn't I stay in? If the baby's sleeping, shouldn't I not come out?

1323
01:07:18,604 --> 01:07:21,704
[Title: 第98問]
[Title: Question 98]

1324
01:07:20,104 --> 01:07:21,204
むずいのじゃ。
This is hard.

1325
01:07:24,054 --> 01:07:25,804
何？ピントか？
What? Focus?

1326
01:07:27,054 --> 01:07:28,154
これ何だ？
What is this?

1327
01:07:29,954 --> 01:07:31,604
あ、写真？はい！
Oh, a photo? Say cheese!

1328
01:07:31,954 --> 01:07:33,654
え、いい写真撮れた！
Whoa, I got a great photo!

1329
01:07:33,704 --> 01:07:35,404
全員が目開けてる！
Everyone has their eyes open!

1330
01:07:35,304 --> 01:07:38,304
[Title: 第99問]
[Title: Question 99]

1331
01:07:35,454 --> 01:07:36,704
わし写真上手かも！
I might be good at photography!

1332
01:07:36,754 --> 01:07:38,004
写真家かも！
Maybe I'm a photographer!

1333
01:07:39,954 --> 01:07:40,504
え？
Huh?

1334
01:07:41,104 --> 01:07:43,554
わしのアルバム来た！アルバム！
My photo album is here! An album!

1335
01:07:44,804 --> 01:07:50,104
[Text: はやいわね。]
[Text: Time flies, doesn't it?]

1336
01:07:45,104 --> 01:07:45,754
え！
Whoa!

1337
01:07:45,804 --> 01:07:49,054
わしが上手に写真撮れたから、あの写真なんじゃない？
Is it using that picture because I took such a good photo?!

1338
01:07:52,004 --> 01:07:53,754
もう3歳だって。
It says I'm already 3 years old.

1339
01:07:53,804 --> 01:07:56,954
あれか！「みんなで空気読み。3」じゃからか！
Oh, I get it! Because it's 'Kuukiyomi 3'!

1340
01:07:58,754 --> 01:08:02,554
私がお母さんできる時間なんて、あっという間に過ぎちゃうのかもね。
The time I get to be a mother might pass by in the blink of an eye.

1341
01:08:02,604 --> 01:08:05,454
切なくてワロタ。人間寿命短いしな。
So bittersweet, lol. Humans have such short lifespans, after all.

1342
01:08:05,554 --> 01:08:07,404
人間の寿命短いしな。
Human lifespans really are short.

1343
01:08:10,854 --> 01:08:12,904
昨日ね、夢を見たのよ。
Yesterday, I had a dream.

1344
01:08:12,954 --> 01:08:13,804
何？
What was it?

1345
01:08:16,954 --> 01:08:20,604
この子が同い年くらいの女の子と、手を繋いでデートしてるの。
You were holding hands and on a date with a girl around your age.

1346
01:08:20,654 --> 01:08:22,904
あ！もしかしてあの彼氏か？
Oh! Could that be that boyfriend?!

1347
01:08:23,004 --> 01:08:25,004
遭難してた彼氏か？
The boyfriend who got stranded?!

1348
01:08:25,104 --> 01:08:26,854
ロボット映画か、恋愛映画か…
A robot movie, or a romance movie...

1349
01:08:26,904 --> 01:08:28,854
あ、1とか2の彼氏か！
Oh, the boyfriend from 1 or 2!

1350
01:08:28,904 --> 01:08:32,404
彼女にひっぱられて結局恋愛映画を見るハメになってるの。
Dragged along by her, you ended up having to watch the romance movie.

1351
01:08:32,454 --> 01:08:33,604
ほうほうほう。
Oh, I see, I see.

1352
01:08:35,004 --> 01:08:38,354
優柔不断なとこ、あなたにそっくりで笑って起きちゃった。
Being so indecisive—you're just like your father, I woke up laughing.

1353
01:08:40,504 --> 01:08:42,954
ええ？私の方に似てるって？そうかなあ…
Huh? Looks more like me? You think so...?

1354
01:08:43,104 --> 01:08:45,754
え！何か過去作の話と繋がってるのじゃ！
Whoa! It's connected to the stories from the previous games!

1355
01:08:46,954 --> 01:08:49,654
この子もいつか空気を読む日が来るのかな。
I wonder if the day will come when you read the room too.

1356
01:08:52,854 --> 01:08:56,154
けれど、今「空気読み」って言葉が悪口としても使…
Though, nowadays 'reading the room' is also used as an insul—

1357
01:08:56,204 --> 01:08:57,954
そうなの！？わしそれ知らない！
Really?! I didn't know that!

1358
01:08:58,754 --> 01:09:03,604
みんなと違えば「空気を読め」。頼みを聞けなきゃ「空気が読めない」って。
If you're different from everyone else, 'read the room.' If you can't do a favor, 'you can't read the room.'

1359
01:09:03,654 --> 01:09:04,904
あ、たまに言われる。
Oh, people tell me that sometimes.

1360
01:09:05,104 --> 01:09:07,704
そりゃ、空気を読むってのは大事なことよ？
Of course, reading the room is an important thing.

1361
01:09:07,904 --> 01:09:08,654
うん。
Yeah.

1362
01:09:11,104 --> 01:09:15,404
でもそれって、人から強要されてしかたなくやることじゃないと思うの。
But I don't think it's something you should be forced into doing reluctantly by others.

1363
01:09:16,604 --> 01:09:17,854
めくんなきゃいけないのか。
Wait, do I have to flip the pages?

1364
01:09:18,004 --> 01:09:20,404
大切なのは…そう、「思いやり」ね。
What's important is... yes, 'thoughtfulness.'

1365
01:09:23,104 --> 01:09:27,554
周りに流されるのではなく、周りの人を思いやって空気が読める…
Not just going with the crowd, but reading the room out of care for those around you...

1366
01:09:29,604 --> 01:09:32,854
芯のある、やさしい強い子に育ってほしいな。
I hope you grow up to be a gentle, strong child with a firm core.

1367
01:09:35,104 --> 01:09:38,004
思いやりをもって読んだ空気は…
When you read the room with thoughtfulness...

1368
01:09:41,704 --> 01:09:46,304
いつかあなたが幸せを掴むとき、あなたの背中を押してくれるはずだから。
One day, when you reach for happiness, it's sure to give you that push forward.

1369
01:09:47,654 --> 01:09:49,104
幸せになりなさい。
Be happy.

1370
01:09:49,654 --> 01:09:50,654
切ない。
So poignant.

1371
01:09:52,204 --> 01:09:53,604
愛情でワロタ。
The pure love, lol.

1372
01:09:54,004 --> 01:09:56,104
なれるわ、あなたなら。
You can do it, if it's you.

1373
01:09:57,204 --> 01:09:58,754
愛情や…
So much love...

1374
01:09:58,904 --> 01:10:00,104
[Text: 私の、自慢の息子ですもの。]
[Text: Because you're my pride and joy, my son.]

1375
01:10:00,112 --> 01:10:03,062
私の、自慢の息子ですもの。
He is my pride and joy of a son, after all.

1376
01:10:06,162 --> 01:10:07,862
ね、愛されててわろた。
Right? It's hilarious how loved he is.

1377
01:10:08,012 --> 01:10:09,862
第100問来た！
Question 100 is here!

1378
01:10:13,312 --> 01:10:14,812
さ、さ、さ、さ。
Here we go, here we go.

1379
01:10:19,962 --> 01:10:20,562
何？
What?

1380
01:10:21,112 --> 01:10:21,762
何？
What?

1381
01:10:21,812 --> 01:10:22,962
何これ？
What is this?

1382
01:10:23,262 --> 01:10:26,262
何この最後のエモそうな演出？
What's with this super emotional-looking scene at the end?

1383
01:10:26,962 --> 01:10:28,612
何最後の
What was that...

1384
01:10:28,662 --> 01:10:31,812
「よくできたわね」みたいな。
like a 'You did a great job' at the end?

1385
01:10:32,062 --> 01:10:33,862
お前が成長した？
'You've grown up'?

1386
01:10:34,012 --> 01:10:38,012
なるほど、おっきくなったんだ！おっきくなって出会ったんだ！
I see, they grew up! They grew up and met each other!

1387
01:10:38,612 --> 01:10:43,312
へぇー…いい世界でわろた。
Whoa... It cracks me up how wholesome this world is.

1388
01:10:43,362 --> 01:10:44,562
ほどよく。
Just right.

1389
01:10:45,312 --> 01:10:52,212
さあ、それではお主ら、あちちめらの結果を見ていくか！
Now then, everyone, shall we take a look at Achichi Mela's results?

1390
01:10:52,562 --> 01:10:53,612
おっと？
Whoa there?

1391
01:10:57,162 --> 01:11:02,712
うーん…
Hmm...

1392
01:11:03,362 --> 01:11:07,612
やっぱ知識が圧倒的に…
As expected, my Knowledge is overwhelmingly...

1393
01:11:08,612 --> 01:11:13,312
知識が圧倒…なんかバランスよく空気読めてないな。
Knowledge is overwhel— Wait, it's like I'm evenly bad at reading the room.

1394
01:11:14,112 --> 01:11:19,712
なんかこれが得意とかがなくて、本当にただ…本当にただ微妙だな！
Like, I don't have a specific strength, it's just really... really mediocre!

1395
01:11:19,962 --> 01:11:22,462
本当に微妙でわろた。
It's honestly hilarious how mediocre it is.

1396
01:11:23,112 --> 01:11:25,212
詳細結果見たい。
I want to see the detailed results.

1397
01:11:25,712 --> 01:11:27,662
あ！詳細結果見れなかった！
Ah! I couldn't see the detailed results!

1398
01:11:28,612 --> 01:11:31,612
できなかった。上手にできなかった。
I couldn't do it. I couldn't do it properly.

1399
01:11:32,112 --> 01:11:34,362
過去のお前で見れないかな？
Can I check it in 'Past You'?

1400
01:11:36,062 --> 01:11:37,412
過去のお前。
'Past You'.

1401
01:11:39,112 --> 01:11:40,112
これや！
This is it!

1402
01:11:42,612 --> 01:11:44,512
Tab！これだ！
Tab! Here it is!

1403
01:11:45,212 --> 01:11:46,412
えー…
Let's see...

1404
01:11:48,912 --> 01:11:51,112
平均よりちょい上。
'Slightly above average.'

1405
01:11:51,112 --> 01:11:52,862
常識力上。
Common sense is above average.

1406
01:11:52,962 --> 01:11:58,612
常識力ちょい上。社会的マナーやエチケットなど。
Common sense is slightly above average. Social manners, etiquette, and such.

1407
01:11:58,862 --> 01:12:07,412
専門知識、一般常識以外のピンポイントな知識の力。知識の引き出しの多さは空気を読むための武器。
Specialized knowledge: pinpoint knowledge outside of general common sense. Having a wide repertoire of knowledge is a weapon for reading the room.

1408
01:12:07,462 --> 01:12:10,712
やっぱ知識の引き出しの多さはあまり…
Yeah, having a wide repertoire of knowledge isn't really my...

1409
01:12:11,462 --> 01:12:17,312
空間認識「良い」。方向感覚の鋭さ。え、ちょっといいんじゃない？「良い」だって！
Spatial awareness: 'Good'. A sharp sense of direction. Hey, isn't that pretty good? It says 'Good'!

1410
01:12:17,512 --> 01:12:22,512
集団力「平均よりちょい上」。チームワークに通ずる協調性。はい、はい、はい。
Group ability: 'Slightly above average'. Cooperativeness leading to teamwork. Yes, yes, yes.

1411
01:12:22,762 --> 01:12:31,612
共感。じんじょう力。「相手の境遇や気持ちを察した行動をとれるかどうか、やさしさ」。はいはいはい。
Empathy. 'Jinjo' power... 'Whether you can act with consideration for others' situations and feelings; kindness.' Right, right, right.

1412
01:12:31,662 --> 01:12:39,312
大人力。「一歩引いて相手を立てたり、他人がやりたがらない役割を進んで担うことで場の雰囲気を良くする気配り」。
Maturity: 'Stepping back to let others shine, or willingly taking on roles others avoid to improve the atmosphere; thoughtfulness.'

1413
01:12:39,312 --> 01:12:42,612
あ、これわし苦手。これわし上手じゃないかも。これ育てたい。
Ah, I'm bad at this. I might not be good at this. I want to improve this.

1414
01:12:42,762 --> 01:12:47,612
にんじょうらしい、にんじょう！じんじょうじゃないらしい。にんじょう！
Apparently it's 'ninjou', ninjou! Not 'jinjou'. Ninjou!

1415
01:12:49,062 --> 01:12:52,062
洞察力、平均よりちょい上。
Insight, slightly above average.

1416
01:12:52,862 --> 01:13:00,512
なんか…何とも言えんな。リズム感、ちょい上。間合い、平均的。
Well... I don't really know what to say. Sense of rhythm, slightly above. Timing, average.

1417
01:13:00,912 --> 01:13:07,262
なるほど。なるほどね…うーん…
I see. I see... Hmm...

1418
01:13:07,712 --> 01:13:13,912
普通の人がどれぐらいなのか分かんないけど、絶望的ではないが良くはないぐらいか。
I don't know what a normal person's score is like, so maybe it's not hopeless, just not great.

1419
01:13:14,312 --> 01:13:17,312
絶望的ではないぐらいか。
Just 'not hopeless,' huh.

1420
01:13:17,862 --> 01:13:30,212
でもゲームで記号化された空気読みがこれなだけで、記号化されていない実生活での空気読みがあんまり、ここまではできないのが課題かな。
But this is just reading the room when it's stylized in a game; in real life where things aren't stylized like this, I can't even do it this well, which is probably my issue.

1421
01:13:30,262 --> 01:13:33,862
これでさ、このゲームってさ、第三者視点で見れるじゃろう？
I mean, in this game, you can view things from a third-person perspective, right?

1422
01:13:33,962 --> 01:13:46,412
第三者視点で冷静に見た上でこれじゃから、自分が実際にその場にいて考えながらやるってのはなかなか…なかなか難しいのでは。
Even when looking calmly from a third-person perspective I get this score, so actually being there in person and thinking on my feet is... pretty tough, isn't it?

1423
01:13:46,462 --> 01:13:49,662
いや、実生活弱いね。わしあんまり上手じゃないんだよな、こういうの。
Man, I'm weak in real life. I'm really not very good at this kind of thing.

1424
01:13:51,512 --> 01:13:56,512
ということでしたのじゃ！「空気読み。3」でしたのじゃー！
And that's how it went! That was 'Kuukiyomi: Consider It! 3'!

1425
01:13:56,562 --> 01:14:02,712
それでは、おしゃべりする場面に戻るのじゃー！のじゃー！
Now then, let's return to the chatting screen!

1426
01:14:04,362 --> 01:14:13,412
うん。やっぱ実生活においての、あのー…処理？処理能力的なところにね、あまり自信がない。
Yeah. When it comes to real life, um... processing? I'm not very confident in my processing ability.

1427
01:14:13,462 --> 01:14:15,562
コメントが動いてにゃいね。
Chat isn't moving, meow.

1428
01:14:15,612 --> 01:14:22,512
頑張れるか、お主。お主頑張れる？お主頑張れるかな？頑張れないかな？ちょっと難しいかな？
Can you do it, little guy? Can you hang in there? Can you do it? Or can't you? Is it a bit too hard?

1429
01:14:22,562 --> 01:14:26,512
コメント欄、空気読めてるか？お主難しいか？
Chat box, are you reading the room? Is it hard for you?

1430
01:14:27,512 --> 01:14:29,612
お！行けるか？
Oh! Can you do it?

1431
01:14:30,112 --> 01:14:33,712
行け…行けないか。
Can you... No, you can't.

1432
01:14:33,762 --> 01:14:37,412
行けないか。しょうがないね。しょうがないよね、そういう時もあるよね。
You can't, huh. It can't be helped. It can't be helped, there are times like that.

1433
01:14:38,312 --> 01:14:40,312
頑張った。「頭いい気がする」。
Good effort. 'I feel like you're smart.'

1434
01:14:40,362 --> 01:14:50,212
いやでもね、なんかね、思うんじゃけどね、わしは自分のことを、あの、言葉にするのは上手だと思うの。いわゆる言語化とかは上手だと思うんじゃけど、
Well, you know, I think I'm good at putting my own thoughts into words. Like, I think I'm good at verbalizing things, but...

1435
01:14:50,262 --> 01:14:59,712
だからと言って、その人の気持ちをね…人の気持ちを分析するのがすごい苦手なんだよなー。すごい苦手。
even so, when it comes to other people's feelings... I'm really bad at analyzing other people's feelings. Really bad at it.

1436
01:15:00,120 --> 01:15:01,470
なんだよな。
...that's just how it is.

1437
01:15:02,170 --> 01:15:03,320
なんか
Like...

1438
01:15:03,320 --> 01:15:09,870
真剣に、わしの能力を、全てを総動員しても、人間が何を考えてるかが本当に分かんなくて
Even if I seriously mobilize every bit of my abilities, I really can't understand what humans are thinking,

1439
01:15:11,120 --> 01:15:12,720
え、難しいね。
Uh, it's tough.

1440
01:15:12,920 --> 01:15:15,420
わしだったらこう考えるなあは分かるんだけどね。
I can understand how I would think in that situation, though.

1441
01:15:15,820 --> 01:15:18,420
他人の視点に立つのがね、難しいのじゃ。
Putting myself in someone else's shoes is what's hard.

1442
01:15:19,920 --> 01:15:21,120
難しい。
It's hard.

1443
01:15:23,120 --> 01:15:26,120
国語の作者の気持ち問題とか苦手？
Am I bad at 'how does the author feel' questions in language class?

1444
01:15:26,320 --> 01:15:30,320
え、作者の気持ちに関しては本文中に答えがあるから難しくないのじゃ。
Well, when it comes to the author's feelings, the answer is right there in the text, so that's not hard.

1445
01:15:31,620 --> 01:15:34,320
うん、なんか、その、分かんない。
Yeah, like, um, I don't know.

1446
01:15:35,120 --> 01:15:43,520
そのさ、学校で習うレベルの文章題とかだったら、その文章題の解き方っていうのがあるから、それに則って解けばいけるんじゃけど、
For reading comprehension questions at the level taught in school, there's a set method for solving them, so as long as I follow that, I can do fine...

1447
01:15:44,520 --> 01:15:47,820
実生活はそうもいかないから難しい、そう。
...but real life doesn't work like that, so it's hard, yeah.

1448
01:15:48,120 --> 01:15:55,720
答え決まってて、その答えがなんでこれになるかみたいなのが論理的に説明されるものならいけるんじゃけど、
If there's a fixed answer and it can be logically explained why that's the answer, I can manage, but...

1449
01:15:56,920 --> 01:16:00,020
道徳ガチ苦手。道徳ガチで苦手。
I'm seriously bad at ethics class. Seriously bad at ethics.

1450
01:16:00,520 --> 01:16:03,720
あの、デビュー前に道徳の教科書読んで勉強したぐらい苦手。
I'm so bad at it that I actually read an ethics textbook to study before my debut.

1451
01:16:03,920 --> 01:16:06,220
勉強したけど、分かんなかった。
I studied it, but I still didn't get it.

1452
01:16:06,320 --> 01:16:07,320
なんか
Like...

1453
01:16:07,320 --> 01:16:15,420
え、それこそ、なんかキョーコとかに、その内容を読んで教えてもらったんだけど、わしにはない発想がキョーコからどんどん出てきてびっくりした。
Even when I had Kyoko read the material and explain it to me, she kept coming up with perspectives I never would've thought of, and it shocked me.

1454
01:16:15,820 --> 01:16:17,920
わしは、分かんなかった。
I just didn't understand.

1455
01:16:18,220 --> 01:16:20,320
道徳のきょ…道徳ガチ苦手。
Ethics class... I'm seriously bad at ethics.

1456
01:16:20,420 --> 01:16:22,520
何考えてるか分かんない。
I have no idea what they're thinking.

1457
01:16:23,020 --> 01:16:24,320
読んだ、読んだ。
I read it, I did.

1458
01:16:25,020 --> 01:16:27,120
感情がガチで苦手。
I'm seriously bad with emotions.

1459
01:16:27,920 --> 01:16:30,320
本当に、ど…道徳心がない。
I really have no... no sense of ethics.

1460
01:16:30,420 --> 01:16:34,420
え、そう、明確な答えがないのが本当に苦手なのじゃ。答えが欲しいの、わしは。
Yeah, right, I really struggle when there's no clear answer. I want an answer.

1461
01:16:34,720 --> 01:16:38,620
答えが欲しいし、答えが言葉になってないとすごい不安なの。不安なんじゃけど、
I want an answer, and if it isn't put into words, I get really anxious. I get anxious, and...

1462
01:16:39,020 --> 01:16:41,620
それがないからすっごい難しいの。
...because there isn't one, it's super hard.

1463
01:16:43,120 --> 01:16:44,720
難しいのじゃ。
It's hard.

1464
01:16:47,620 --> 01:16:50,320
得意な教科？得意な教科あったかな？
A subject I'm good at? Did I have a subject I was good at?

1465
01:16:51,920 --> 01:16:56,520
なんだろ。帰国子女だから、周りよりは英語は良かったかもしれないけど。
Let's see. Since I'm a returnee, my English might have been better than the people around me, though.

1466
01:16:58,120 --> 01:17:03,020
え、そう、人の心がないんかなの。わし、多分人の心がないの。分かんないの。
Yeah, maybe I just don't have a human heart. I probably don't have a human heart. I don't get it.

1467
01:17:03,320 --> 01:17:04,520
分かんないのじゃ。
I don't understand.

1468
01:17:04,620 --> 01:17:05,820
最近の課題。
My recent struggle.

1469
01:17:07,120 --> 01:17:09,020
「なんとなく分かったりしない？」
"Don't you kind of just get it?"

1470
01:17:09,220 --> 01:17:12,720
いや、その「なんとなく分かる」が本当に分かんない。
No, that "kind of just getting it" is what I really don't understand.

1471
01:17:12,920 --> 01:17:13,820
なんか
Like...

1472
01:17:14,020 --> 01:17:22,020
後から言われて、納得はしないけど、覚える、暗記する。
When someone tells me afterward, I don't necessarily feel convinced, but I remember it—I memorize it.

1473
01:17:22,320 --> 01:17:29,520
「あ、これをすると人間こういう気持ちになるんだ」みたいなので、一問一答で、覚える。けど、
Like, "Oh, if I do this, humans feel this way," and I memorize it like flashcards. But...

1474
01:17:31,120 --> 01:17:35,920
一問一答で覚えてるだけだから、応用ができないのじゃ。分かんないの。
...because I only memorize it as one-to-one Q&A, I can't apply it to other situations. I don't get it.

1475
01:17:36,320 --> 01:17:37,320
難しい。
It's hard.

1476
01:17:37,620 --> 01:17:40,320
「じゃあなんで正解を探そうとする？」不安だから。
"Then why do you try to find the right answer?" Because I'm anxious.

1477
01:17:40,520 --> 01:17:42,920
正解が分かんないと不安なのじゃ。
I get anxious if I don't know the right answer.

1478
01:17:43,020 --> 01:17:47,820
分からないことが本当に不安で、ざわざわするの、心が。
Not knowing makes me really anxious, and my heart feels restless.

1479
01:17:48,520 --> 01:17:50,620
だから、知りたいのじゃ。
That's why I want to know.

1480
01:17:53,120 --> 01:17:57,120
人の心分かろうが怖い？でも人間結構分からない？結構人間分かる？
It's scary to understand human hearts? Wait, don't humans also not get it? Or do humans get it pretty well?

1481
01:17:58,720 --> 01:18:02,120
ロボットでいらっしゃる？え、サラマンダーなのじゃ。わしはサラマンダー。
"Are you a robot?" Hey, I'm a salamander! I am a salamander.

1482
01:18:03,220 --> 01:18:05,920
分かんないの。分かんないの。
I don't get it. I don't get it.

1483
01:18:08,620 --> 01:18:19,120
人の心を暗記？え、でも、え、人の心は暗記じゃないけど、コミュニケーションで、なんか「これを言って、こう言うと不快になるらしいからやめよう」みたいな感じで暗記はして覚えてる。
Memorizing human hearts? Well, I don't memorize human hearts per se, but for communication, I memorize things like, "Apparently saying this or phrasing it that way makes people uncomfortable, so let's avoid it."

1484
01:18:19,320 --> 01:18:22,520
うん。なんか、トラブルがあった時しか解決できないけどね。
Yeah. Though I can only figure it out when trouble actually happens.

1485
01:18:22,820 --> 01:18:26,820
なんか「これがダメらしい」ってのは一問一答で覚えていってるけど。
I've been memorizing things like "apparently this isn't okay" one by one, though.

1486
01:18:27,120 --> 01:18:28,220
難しいのじゃ。
It's hard.

1487
01:18:30,720 --> 01:18:35,920
「マニュアルあると安心する？」え、するするする！ガチで全員マニュアルを提出してほしいのじゃ。
"Do you feel relieved if there's a manual?" Yes, yes, yes! I seriously want everyone to submit a manual.

1488
01:18:36,320 --> 01:18:45,120
あの、人間と関わる時に説明書を渡した方がお互いコミュニケーションが円滑になるかなと思って、自分の説明書を作ったことがあるんじゃけど、
I thought handing over an instruction manual when interacting with humans would make communication smoother for both sides, so I once made a manual for myself...

1489
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:52,820
そう、「これをすると喜ぶし、これが嫌だ」みたいな、そういうのをスプレッドシートにまとめて、友達に渡そうとしたことがあるんだけど、
Yeah, like "doing this makes me happy and I hate this," I put all that in a spreadsheet and tried to give it to a friend...

1490
01:18:53,220 --> 01:19:02,220
すっごい仲良い友達にそれをやったら、ま、すごい仲良いからいいけど、なんかあんま関係値がない人にこれはやんない方がいいって怒られたのじゃ。
...and when I did that with a super close friend, they said it's fine since we're super close, but scolded me that I shouldn't do that with people I don't have much of a relationship with yet.

1491
01:19:03,320 --> 01:19:05,420
うん。え、でもわしは欲しいの。
Yeah. Well, I still want one, though.

1492
01:19:05,520 --> 01:19:09,220
別にわしは見せなくてもいいけど、わしは欲しいの。渡されたいの。
I don't necessarily have to show mine, but I want one. I want to be handed one.

1493
01:19:10,120 --> 01:19:16,820
別に自分がみせて、相手がそれを叶えてくれる必要はないんだけど、
It's not like I need to show mine and have the other person accommodate everything...

1494
01:19:16,920 --> 01:19:17,920
ないんだけど、
...I don't need that, but...

1495
01:19:21,620 --> 01:19:25,320
相手が「これされたら嫌だ」みたいなのは全部知りたいのじゃ。
...I want to know everything about what the other person dislikes having done to them.

1496
01:19:25,920 --> 01:19:29,320
教えてほしい。できるだけ嫌な気持ちさせたくないから。
I want them to tell me. Because I want to avoid making them feel bad as much as possible.

1497
01:19:29,620 --> 01:19:31,320
欲しいんだよなあ。
I really want one.

1498
01:19:32,420 --> 01:19:33,620
難しいのじゃ。
It's hard.

1499
01:19:35,020 --> 01:19:39,020
「そんなに悩むのになんでホロ選んだの？」え、仲間に入れた欲しかった。
"Why did you choose Hololive if you struggle with that so much?" Well, I wanted to be part of a group.

1500
01:19:39,320 --> 01:19:41,420
仲間に入れて欲しかったのじゃ。
I wanted to be let into the group.

1501
01:19:42,020 --> 01:19:44,520
居場所が欲しかったのじゃ、わしも。
I wanted a place where I belonged too.

1502
01:19:44,720 --> 01:19:49,620
うん。なんか仲間に入れてもらうの苦手だから、練習したいって思ったの。
Yeah. I'm bad at fitting into groups, so I thought I wanted to practice.

1503
01:19:50,120 --> 01:19:50,720
うん。
Yeah.

1504
01:19:53,620 --> 01:19:55,220
そう、いや、難しい。
Right, well, it's hard.

1505
01:19:55,420 --> 01:20:00,020
説明書じゃ測れない？そうなの？説明書あった方が絶対いいやろって思うんだけど。
You can't measure it with a manual? Really? I feel like having a manual would definitely be better, though.

1506
01:20:00,928 --> 01:20:10,428
思うんだけど、なんか人間はあんまりそういう説明書とか、なんか自分を説明したりされたりするのが好きじゃないらしいから、あの、お蔵入りになったのじゃ。
I think humans don't really seem to like manuals or explaining themselves or having themselves explained, so, um, that got shelved noja.

1507
01:20:10,428 --> 01:20:12,228
うん、お蔵入りになった。
Yeah, it got shelved.

1508
01:20:13,328 --> 01:20:14,328
そう。
Right.

1509
01:20:17,328 --> 01:20:18,428
難しい。
It's hard.

1510
01:20:24,428 --> 01:20:25,328
うん。
Yeah.

1511
01:20:29,928 --> 01:20:33,628
説明つかないことだらけ。
It's full of things that can't be explained.

1512
01:20:33,928 --> 01:20:46,928
人間わかんないよ、わし。わかんないけど、あんまり傷つけたくないし、できるだけ楽しいなって思ってほしいから、できるだけ寄り添いたいが…寄り添いたいが、
I don't understand humans. I don't, but I don't want to hurt anyone, and I want everyone to have as much fun as possible, so I want to be there for you... I want to be considerate, but...

1513
01:20:46,928 --> 01:20:48,128
難しい。
It's difficult.

1514
01:20:49,128 --> 01:20:58,028
努力はしているつもりなんじゃけど、努力の方向性が合ってないと努力ってあんま意味ないから、で、わしは自分に対してそれが起こっているかも。
I feel like I'm trying my best noja, but if your effort isn't pointed in the right direction it doesn't mean much, and I think that might be happening with me.

1515
01:20:59,128 --> 01:20:59,928
うん。
Yeah.

1516
01:21:00,328 --> 01:21:01,728
む、むずいのじゃ。
I-It's tough noja.

1517
01:21:03,428 --> 01:21:09,128
から、あの、ちょっとずつね、慣れたい。ちょっとずつ慣れたいって思ってるのじゃ。
So, um, little by little, I want to get used to it. I'm hoping to get used to it bit by bit noja.

1518
01:21:10,828 --> 01:21:14,128
「わかんないのが楽しいと思わない？」え、わかんない。
"Don't you think not knowing is part of the fun?" Huh, I don't know.

1519
01:21:14,428 --> 01:21:17,528
不安なの。わかんないのが本当に不安なのじゃ。
It makes me anxious. Not knowing really makes me anxious noja.

1520
01:21:18,228 --> 01:21:20,128
全部わかっておきたい。
I want to understand everything beforehand.

1521
01:21:21,628 --> 01:21:25,128
ざわざわするの。わからないことに対して。
I feel uneasy... about things I don't understand.

1522
01:21:26,528 --> 01:21:27,328
うん。
Yeah.

1523
01:21:28,228 --> 01:21:29,928
から頑張りたいのじゃ。
So I want to try my best noja.

1524
01:21:30,728 --> 01:21:31,528
うん。
Yeah.

1525
01:21:35,628 --> 01:21:37,628
人間のこと知りたい。
I want to learn about humans.

1526
01:21:38,328 --> 01:21:44,528
「知れた時嬉しくない？」え、知れたら嬉しい。ドパれます。知るっていうことはドパれます。
"Isn't it nice when you learn something?" Oh, learning things makes me happy. It gives me a dopamine rush. Knowing things gives me a dopamine rush.

1527
01:21:45,328 --> 01:21:46,128
うん。
Yeah.

1528
01:21:47,828 --> 01:21:52,828
うん、慣れていきたい。慣れていきたいなと思うのじゃ。
Yeah, I want to get used to it. I want to gradually get used to it noja.

1529
01:21:53,128 --> 01:22:04,328
「全部わかったら楽しくない？」全部わかることは一生起こらないのじゃ。わからないことが多すぎて。だから、それはわかんない前提なんじゃない？どうなんじゃろ。
"Wouldn't it be boring if you knew everything?" Knowing everything is never going to happen noja. There are just too many unknowns. So isn't that already assuming I won't know everything? Wonder how that works noja.

1530
01:22:05,428 --> 01:22:06,228
うん。
Yeah.

1531
01:22:08,228 --> 01:22:15,528
「傷つくこと怖がりすぎてる？」傷つきたくないよ。傷つけたくないし、傷つきたくないし。
"Are you too afraid of getting hurt?" I don't want to get hurt! I don't want to hurt anyone, and I don't want to get hurt either.

1532
01:22:16,928 --> 01:22:17,728
うん。
Yeah.

1533
01:22:20,828 --> 01:22:21,628
うん。
Yeah.

1534
01:22:23,128 --> 01:22:26,728
「覚悟を持つ」覚悟ね〜。
"Have resolve." Resolve, huh...

1535
01:22:29,128 --> 01:22:32,128
覚悟がないのかな、わし。
Maybe I'm lacking resolve.

1536
01:22:33,828 --> 01:22:37,828
うん、まあちょっとずつですのじゃ。ちょっとずつですのじゃ。
Yeah, well, it's one step at a time noja. One step at a time noja.

1537
01:22:39,328 --> 01:22:40,128
うん。
Yeah.

1538
01:22:45,128 --> 01:22:48,628
うん、コミュニケーションね、学んでいきたい気持ちあり。
Yeah, communication, right... I definitely want to keep learning it.

1539
01:22:49,128 --> 01:22:53,928
最近の課題。最近の課題、コミュニケーションなのじゃ。
My current goal. My current challenge is communication noja.

1540
01:22:54,428 --> 01:22:56,928
徐々に。徐々にね。
Gradually. Gradually, you know.

1541
01:23:00,128 --> 01:23:05,928
経験値をね、積みたい。積みたいのじゃ。
I want to build up experience points. I want to gain experience noja.

1542
01:23:05,928 --> 01:23:07,728
空気読み全クリする。
I'll clear all of Kuukiyomi.

1543
01:23:08,128 --> 01:23:15,928
空気読み、また、まだ続きあるっぽい。まだ続きあるっぽいから、それもいずれやりたいのじゃ。
It looks like there's still more to Kuukiyomi. Since there's more, I want to play that too eventually noja.

1544
01:23:17,028 --> 01:23:20,728
「ホロに来た時点で覚悟はめっちゃ大きい」うん、おっきい。
"Just joining hololive took huge resolve." Yeah, it was huge.

1545
01:23:21,628 --> 01:23:34,328
でもなんかわしがした覚悟って、たくさんの人に見られる覚悟はしてきたけど、人間と関わる覚悟はそこまでちゃんとできてなかったかもって思うから、そこをもっと頑張りたいな。
But I feel like the resolve I had was to be seen by lots of people, and maybe I hadn't properly prepared myself for interacting closely with humans, so I want to work harder on that.

1546
01:23:34,328 --> 01:23:34,928
うん。
Yeah.

1547
01:23:35,328 --> 01:23:36,928
そう、まだあるっぽい。
Right, it seems there's more.

1548
01:23:37,028 --> 01:23:52,628
ちょ、一旦ね、一旦空気読みで社会の、あの、パターンを学んで…初級編じゃろ？まず初級じゃろ？初級を学んで、実践編・応用編として、その配信で学んでいくということですのじゃ。
So for now, I'll learn the patterns of society through Kuukiyomi... That's the beginner course, right? Beginner first! After learning the basics, I'll take on the practical and advanced courses through streaming noja.

1549
01:23:53,128 --> 01:23:55,128
うん。頑張るのじゃ。
Yeah. I'll do my best noja.

1550
01:23:56,528 --> 01:23:57,228
うん。
Yeah.

1551
01:23:59,128 --> 01:24:01,128
頑張ろうと思いますのじゃ。
I intend to give it my all noja.

1552
01:24:02,328 --> 01:24:03,128
うん。
Yeah.

1553
01:24:04,828 --> 01:24:11,728
ということで、今日の配信はおしまいなのじゃー！
And with that, today's stream is all wrapped up noja!

1554
01:24:12,428 --> 01:24:22,528
明日は？明日は？明日コラボや！ホラゲか？明日ホラゲか？明日きょうことホラゲの予感。
Tomorrow? Tomorrow is... A collab tomorrow! Is it a horror game? Horror game tomorrow? I have a feeling it's a horror game with Kyoko tomorrow.

1555
01:24:22,828 --> 01:24:32,928
ホラーゲームするのじゃ！週1の！やっていこうと思うので、お楽しみになのじゃー！
We're playing a horror game noja! The weekly one! Looking forward to doing that, so stay tuned noja!

1556
01:24:33,128 --> 01:24:40,328
それではお主ら、さらばじゃー！
Well then, everyone, farewell noja!

1557
01:24:42,628 --> 01:25:00,128
